1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,461
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,545 --> 00:00:08,299
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

3
00:00:08,383 --> 00:00:10,760
- <i>♪ Fix it</i> ♪
- <i>♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:12,846
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

5
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:20,603
You're the one who picked up Ibyang
the other day, right?

7
00:00:20,687 --> 00:00:23,982
- How is she?
- She's been crying for several nights.

8
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:25,525
Can I see her?

9
00:00:25,608 --> 00:00:28,611
[in English] Viktor Petrov,
ambassador of Zahran.

10
00:00:28,695 --> 00:00:31,531
[Atoy, in English] <i>Mr. Ambassador,</i>
<i>I am Alexei Sokolov.</i>

11
00:00:31,614 --> 00:00:34,576
[Mercado] <i>If you have the chance</i>
<i>to get it now, do it.</i>

12
00:00:34,659 --> 00:00:36,870
<i>But make sure you won't be compromised.</i>

13
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:43,877
PREVIOUSLY

14
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:45,044
[Samir] Hey!

15
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:47,756
[in English] Sir, you are acting
very suspicious.

16
00:00:47,839 --> 00:00:49,466
[in English] I will have to tell
the ambassador.

17
00:00:49,549 --> 00:00:50,383
- [grunts]
- [Kurt gasps]

18
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:51,634
[Viktor, in Russian] <i>What happened here?</i>

19
00:00:51,718 --> 00:00:54,179
[in English] This man…
This man harassed me!

20
00:00:54,262 --> 00:00:55,096
[in English] Let's go.

21
00:00:55,180 --> 00:00:56,514
[Kurt, in English] <i>Emerson,</i>
<i>you should have seen it!</i>

22
00:00:56,598 --> 00:00:58,933
[in English] It was amazing!
We almost got caught!

23
00:00:59,017 --> 00:01:01,561
- Go shampoo your hair. It'll come off.
- [in English] Okay.

24
00:01:01,644 --> 00:01:05,815
Brother Atoy is so kind to us,
he needs to know the truth.

25
00:01:05,899 --> 00:01:09,527
Do you really want
to repay his kindness with pain?

26
00:01:09,611 --> 00:01:12,280
Karla, I'm begging you.

27
00:01:12,363 --> 00:01:14,532
Don't tell him anything.

28
00:01:14,616 --> 00:01:17,744
The question now is,
how do we extract the laptop?

29
00:01:17,827 --> 00:01:20,955
If it's hard to enter the building
from the inside,

30
00:01:21,998 --> 00:01:23,124
I'll do it from the outside.

31
00:01:29,255 --> 00:01:31,174
- [Kurt] Oh.
- [music fades]

32
00:01:31,257 --> 00:01:33,676
- [Karla] Thank you, brother.
- You're welcome!

33
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:41,768
[sneaky music playing]

34
00:01:41,851 --> 00:01:43,186
[in English] Uncanny.

35
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:46,397
Brother, one order, takeout.

36
00:01:48,274 --> 00:01:51,319
[in English] Karla,
did Atoy teach you that style?

37
00:01:51,402 --> 00:01:54,364
[in English] Because that's exactly
how he prepares his pares.

38
00:01:54,447 --> 00:01:56,825
No. This is just how I like it.

39
00:01:56,908 --> 00:01:58,159
[in English] Weird.

40
00:01:58,743 --> 00:02:00,954
[in English] You know, I've served
so many pares,

41
00:02:01,037 --> 00:02:03,289
and, uh, besides Atoy,

42
00:02:03,373 --> 00:02:05,959
I think you're the only one
I've ever seen who does it like that.

43
00:02:06,042 --> 00:02:07,627
[in English] It's almost like, uh…

44
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:10,421
[in English] It's like, uh…
You're almost like brother and sister.

45
00:02:10,505 --> 00:02:11,422
Right? [chuckles]

46
00:02:11,506 --> 00:02:13,591
- [Kurt] Right?
- [Nestor] Uh-huh.

47
00:02:13,675 --> 00:02:14,801
[Nestor] You said it,

48
00:02:14,884 --> 00:02:17,637
Brother Kurt. You'd really think
Atoy is Karla's brother.

49
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:18,721
Mmm-hmm.

50
00:02:20,390 --> 00:02:23,560
Look, they even have the same eyes.

51
00:02:24,310 --> 00:02:26,938
- [Tukmol] You're right.
- Stop it already!

52
00:02:27,021 --> 00:02:28,731
He's not my brother! You're so annoying!

53
00:02:29,941 --> 00:02:31,776
Brother Kurt, wrap this up for me.

54
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:33,153
I'll just eat at home.

55
00:02:33,236 --> 00:02:34,445
I need to buy something at the store.

56
00:02:34,529 --> 00:02:35,446
I'll come back for it.

57
00:02:35,530 --> 00:02:38,408
[music fades]

58
00:02:38,491 --> 00:02:40,827
Karla is so moody. She's baffling.

59
00:02:40,910 --> 00:02:43,121
Just like Atoy when he sulks.

60
00:02:43,204 --> 00:02:44,747
[laughs]

61
00:02:44,831 --> 00:02:46,624
- Psst, hey!
- No, it's true.

62
00:02:46,708 --> 00:02:47,792
Pass me that-- This one.

63
00:02:48,626 --> 00:02:50,044
[suave theme music playing]

64
00:02:50,128 --> 00:02:51,963
[motorcycle revving]

65
00:02:52,046 --> 00:02:52,922
[sewing machine whirring]

66
00:02:53,006 --> 00:02:53,882
[scratches]

67
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:55,884
[snipping]

68
00:02:56,509 --> 00:02:59,762
[sewing machine clacking]

69
00:02:59,846 --> 00:03:01,472
- [gun cocks]
- [gunshots]

70
00:03:01,556 --> 00:03:02,640
[gunshots]

71
00:03:02,724 --> 00:03:03,933
[clacking]

72
00:03:04,017 --> 00:03:05,435
[clicking]

73
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:07,520
[snipping]

74
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:13,276
[electronic blipping]

75
00:03:15,236 --> 00:03:16,863
- [Ame] Ibyang!
- Hmm?

76
00:03:16,946 --> 00:03:17,989
[Ame] Hey, Ibyang!

77
00:03:18,072 --> 00:03:21,492
- [Cita sighs] Ibyang!
- Stop what you're doing.

78
00:03:21,576 --> 00:03:24,203
We have a surprise for you!

79
00:03:24,287 --> 00:03:25,455
What is it?

80
00:03:25,538 --> 00:03:26,831
[Cita giggles]

81
00:03:29,125 --> 00:03:31,127
[Cita sighs]

82
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:34,213
[Audrey] Hi, Ibyang.

83
00:03:34,297 --> 00:03:38,843
[light music playing]

84
00:03:38,927 --> 00:03:39,928
Hi.

85
00:03:42,597 --> 00:03:47,018
I heard that… dumplings are your favorite.

86
00:03:48,978 --> 00:03:49,812
So…

87
00:03:49,896 --> 00:03:52,190
[paper rustling]

88
00:03:52,273 --> 00:03:54,359
I brought some for you.

89
00:03:54,442 --> 00:03:56,277
Oh? What do you say, child?

90
00:03:58,905 --> 00:04:01,157
Thank you, but…

91
00:04:01,741 --> 00:04:03,952
dumplings aren't my favorite anymore.

92
00:04:04,035 --> 00:04:06,704
[melancholic music playing]

93
00:04:06,788 --> 00:04:07,914
[Audrey] Really?

94
00:04:10,124 --> 00:04:11,542
Since when?

95
00:04:13,586 --> 00:04:14,837
Just now.

96
00:04:16,881 --> 00:04:19,050
- You've earned a lot today.
- [indistinct]

97
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:20,635
Good thing the noisy ones are gone.

98
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:23,596
- [Kurt] Karla.
- Brother Kurt, my order.

99
00:04:23,680 --> 00:04:26,474
Hey, uh, I'm really sorry
for what I said earlier,

100
00:04:26,557 --> 00:04:29,602
about you and Atoy
being like brother and sister.

101
00:04:30,353 --> 00:04:31,562
It's fine, Brother Kurt.

102
00:04:32,897 --> 00:04:34,107
Wait.

103
00:04:34,607 --> 00:04:36,192
Then why did you get mad?

104
00:04:36,776 --> 00:04:39,195
Don't you want Atoy to be your brother?

105
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:41,322
Atoy is so kind to you.

106
00:04:41,406 --> 00:04:42,282
[sighs]

107
00:04:42,365 --> 00:04:46,452
If I didn't know you,
I'd really think you were siblings.

108
00:04:46,536 --> 00:04:50,373
Honestly, Brother Atoy
is the best brother in the whole world.

109
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:54,460
Anyone would be lucky to be his sibling.

110
00:04:54,544 --> 00:04:57,755
- But--
- Oh, so what's the problem?

111
00:04:58,673 --> 00:05:02,010
It's okay, but… Not really.

112
00:05:02,093 --> 00:05:02,969
It's complicated.

113
00:05:03,052 --> 00:05:04,721
[pensive music playing]

114
00:05:04,804 --> 00:05:09,475
I wish he were, but…
you shouldn't just wish for things.

115
00:05:09,976 --> 00:05:11,019
There are consequences.

116
00:05:11,102 --> 00:05:13,354
[in English] Wait, but…
What are you trying to say?

117
00:05:13,438 --> 00:05:15,565
[in English] Because I'm-- I'm confused.

118
00:05:15,648 --> 00:05:16,816
Actually, me too.

119
00:05:16,899 --> 00:05:18,318
It's hard to explain.

120
00:05:18,401 --> 00:05:21,779
Oh, Karla, don't think
about it anymore, okay?

121
00:05:21,863 --> 00:05:26,117
Forget it, because
you're not really Atoy's sister.

122
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:30,246
The one to pity here is Ibyang.

123
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:32,790
Doesn't she live with Ame at your place?

124
00:05:32,874 --> 00:05:33,750
[in English] Really?

125
00:05:33,833 --> 00:05:35,585
[in English] I thought
they were with Atoy.

126
00:05:35,668 --> 00:05:36,961
[Siony] Oh, not anymore!

127
00:05:37,045 --> 00:05:41,507
I heard Atoy won't adopt Ibyang

128
00:05:41,591 --> 00:05:43,926
because he already has his own child.

129
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:47,305
And he reconciled
with the mother of that child.

130
00:05:47,388 --> 00:05:49,807
So Ibyang is left out.

131
00:05:49,891 --> 00:05:51,893
- What's the name of that woman again?
- [Kurt] Oh.

132
00:05:51,976 --> 00:05:53,936
[in English] You had all that gossip,
but you forgot the name?

133
00:05:54,020 --> 00:05:56,314
Oh, I'm not a gossipmonger! [chuckles]

134
00:05:56,397 --> 00:05:57,607
It's Ms. Audrey.

135
00:05:57,690 --> 00:05:59,025
Ah, that's it.

136
00:05:59,108 --> 00:06:01,027
I really feel sorry for Ibyang.

137
00:06:01,110 --> 00:06:03,988
She really wanted
Brother Atoy to adopt her.

138
00:06:04,072 --> 00:06:05,573
Mm-hmm.

139
00:06:05,656 --> 00:06:06,574
[music fades]

140
00:06:06,657 --> 00:06:08,451
I'll go ahead.

141
00:06:08,534 --> 00:06:12,997
[somber music playing]

142
00:06:19,754 --> 00:06:21,005
Ibyang…

143
00:06:24,675 --> 00:06:28,429
I know you were hurt…

144
00:06:31,474 --> 00:06:33,559
and upset with me.

145
00:06:39,107 --> 00:06:40,608
[in English] And I'm sorry.

146
00:06:40,691 --> 00:06:42,318
[melancholic music playing]

147
00:06:42,401 --> 00:06:44,403
[sobs, in English] I'm sorry.

148
00:06:52,662 --> 00:06:54,288
[Audrey, in English] I'm sorry.

149
00:06:57,917 --> 00:06:59,752
I hope… [sighs]

150
00:07:00,419 --> 00:07:01,963
you can forgive me.

151
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:08,761
Because I missed you.

152
00:07:12,432 --> 00:07:14,559
I missed you, Ibyang.

153
00:07:17,019 --> 00:07:19,063
I missed you too.

154
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:21,941
Really?

155
00:07:22,024 --> 00:07:23,568
- [music fades]
- [soft chuckle]

156
00:07:23,651 --> 00:07:28,364
[sentimental music playing]

157
00:07:33,161 --> 00:07:34,078
[sobs]

158
00:07:51,387 --> 00:07:53,181
[traffic noises]

159
00:07:55,558 --> 00:07:57,435
- Audrey.
- Hi!

160
00:07:58,394 --> 00:08:00,938
What-- What are you doing here?

161
00:08:01,022 --> 00:08:02,607
Are you… Are you alone?

162
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:03,733
No, I'm with someone.

163
00:08:03,816 --> 00:08:07,778
Um, Miss Cita
just stepped out for a while.

164
00:08:07,862 --> 00:08:09,113
- Ah.
- [in English] Actually…

165
00:08:09,197 --> 00:08:11,324
[pensive music playing]

166
00:08:11,407 --> 00:08:13,701
I've been waiting for you.

167
00:08:17,914 --> 00:08:19,207
Oh, uh…

168
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:21,042
How… How are you?

169
00:08:21,542 --> 00:08:23,085
- Um…
- What…

170
00:08:23,169 --> 00:08:24,921
- There's--
- I'm okay. You?

171
00:08:25,004 --> 00:08:27,006
You look tired.

172
00:08:27,757 --> 00:08:29,175
Are you okay?

173
00:08:30,635 --> 00:08:31,469
Mm-hmm.

174
00:08:32,053 --> 00:08:33,221
Um…

175
00:08:34,555 --> 00:08:35,973
Have you eaten?

176
00:08:36,933 --> 00:08:39,185
Maybe you want to have dinner?

177
00:08:39,268 --> 00:08:41,187
Uh, shall we have dinner?

178
00:08:41,270 --> 00:08:43,356
Uh, Audrey, well…

179
00:08:44,273 --> 00:08:45,942
Excuse me, um…

180
00:08:46,025 --> 00:08:48,069
I can't because…

181
00:08:48,152 --> 00:08:49,904
I have work.

182
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:52,281
Sorry.

183
00:08:55,993 --> 00:08:57,036
Atoy…

184
00:08:57,119 --> 00:09:00,206
[music fades]

185
00:09:00,289 --> 00:09:01,624
Do we have a problem?

186
00:09:01,707 --> 00:09:07,338
[suspicious music playing]

187
00:09:07,421 --> 00:09:08,881
[Dmitri, in English]
<i>You seem like a good father.</i>

188
00:09:09,465 --> 00:09:11,717
[in English] But I don't want you
around my daughter,

189
00:09:12,510 --> 00:09:14,136
much less marrying her

190
00:09:15,763 --> 00:09:18,015
or building a family with her.

191
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:22,186
I don't want Audrey to think
I'm separating you.

192
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:24,981
[in English] But I know
what's best for her.

193
00:09:26,691 --> 00:09:28,109
And it's not you.

194
00:09:29,694 --> 00:09:32,655
[sighs]

195
00:09:33,406 --> 00:09:35,199
[music fades]

196
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:37,118
That night I went to your house…

197
00:09:37,201 --> 00:09:39,328
[pensive music playing]

198
00:09:39,412 --> 00:09:41,455
When we had dinner.

199
00:09:42,915 --> 00:09:44,750
Your father talked to me.

200
00:09:48,671 --> 00:09:49,839
[in English] In short…

201
00:09:55,177 --> 00:09:57,013
He wants me to stay away from you.

202
00:10:02,435 --> 00:10:04,270
Why didn't you tell me?

203
00:10:04,770 --> 00:10:07,023
Because you didn't need to know.

204
00:10:08,065 --> 00:10:09,066
What for?

205
00:10:10,151 --> 00:10:14,196
We're both adults. We know what we want.

206
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:16,198
And I know what I want.

207
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,243
Do you?

208
00:10:19,327 --> 00:10:22,371
[somber music playing]

209
00:10:26,917 --> 00:10:31,547
I know what I want too, Atoy.

210
00:10:38,012 --> 00:10:39,305
Thank you.

211
00:10:42,266 --> 00:10:43,309
Thank you.

212
00:10:44,560 --> 00:10:45,853
At least now…

213
00:10:47,563 --> 00:10:52,526
I feel more at ease
because I know what you want.

214
00:10:55,738 --> 00:10:59,408
Next time, if we have a problem…

215
00:11:00,993 --> 00:11:01,952
send me a text.

216
00:11:03,579 --> 00:11:05,748
I understand you're busy.

217
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:10,961
[chuckles softly]

218
00:11:13,339 --> 00:11:16,217
[sentimental music playing]

219
00:11:16,801 --> 00:11:18,469
[Cita] Looks like… [chuckles softly]

220
00:11:18,552 --> 00:11:19,678
you've made up.

221
00:11:20,179 --> 00:11:21,138
[chuckles]

222
00:11:21,931 --> 00:11:23,516
Did you tell her?

223
00:11:24,016 --> 00:11:27,603
He already told me
what he and Dad talked about.

224
00:11:27,686 --> 00:11:30,147
[music fades]

225
00:11:31,065 --> 00:11:33,442
Godmother, where's Karla?

226
00:11:33,526 --> 00:11:35,611
I've been calling her.
She's not answering.

227
00:11:35,694 --> 00:11:37,405
Even by text.

228
00:11:37,488 --> 00:11:39,281
I have a job I want to give her.

229
00:11:39,990 --> 00:11:41,992
[Cita] Hmm…

230
00:11:42,076 --> 00:11:43,744
Uh, maybe she's busy.

231
00:11:44,245 --> 00:11:45,162
[Atoy] Busy?

232
00:11:45,246 --> 00:11:46,497
[pensive music playing]

233
00:11:46,580 --> 00:11:48,457
What job are you giving Karla?

234
00:11:49,792 --> 00:11:52,711
Karla usually drives me when I have a gig.

235
00:11:52,795 --> 00:11:56,006
Usually, when I call her,
she answers quickly.

236
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:57,675
But now, it's like…

237
00:11:58,467 --> 00:12:00,094
Maybe she really is busy.

238
00:12:00,177 --> 00:12:03,389
That's why I'm worried
who I'll call instead.

239
00:12:07,768 --> 00:12:10,062
- [music fades]
- [sighs]

240
00:12:10,146 --> 00:12:12,064
Hmm? I'm game.

241
00:12:12,148 --> 00:12:13,691
When is it? I can do it now.

242
00:12:13,774 --> 00:12:16,735
Eh, Emerson, just a warning, okay.

243
00:12:16,819 --> 00:12:19,155
What we're about to do is dangerous.

244
00:12:19,238 --> 00:12:23,325
The national security
of our country depends on this.

245
00:12:24,034 --> 00:12:26,328
You can't fail. Do you understand?

246
00:12:26,412 --> 00:12:28,164
[Atoy] <i>Failure is not allowed.</i>

247
00:12:28,247 --> 00:12:29,790
<i>I might not come back.</i>

248
00:12:30,416 --> 00:12:33,210
We'll defend the country. I'll be a hero.

249
00:12:34,044 --> 00:12:36,672
A hero, but in the grave.

250
00:12:37,256 --> 00:12:39,800
That won't happen! Not with you!

251
00:12:39,884 --> 00:12:41,135
[in English] I got your back, bro!

252
00:12:41,218 --> 00:12:43,387
We can do this. Let's claim it!

253
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:45,055
Just make sure.

254
00:12:46,015 --> 00:12:48,100
Because I don't want to leave
my loved ones behind.

255
00:12:49,643 --> 00:12:50,811
Prepare yourself.

256
00:12:50,895 --> 00:12:54,899
[rock music playing]

257
00:12:54,982 --> 00:12:58,110
[muffled chattering in the distance]

258
00:13:06,118 --> 00:13:06,994
Ibyang!

259
00:13:08,245 --> 00:13:11,081
Look at this student, very cute.

260
00:13:11,165 --> 00:13:13,792
Here. Uh, your lunch.

261
00:13:14,376 --> 00:13:16,921
Uh, Tatoy prepared this for you.

262
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:21,509
[somber music playing]

263
00:13:23,385 --> 00:13:25,721
Uh… Here, take this.

264
00:13:25,804 --> 00:13:29,266
Uh… He said…

265
00:13:30,434 --> 00:13:34,104
you should do well in school, and…

266
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:35,981
don't get into fights, okay?

267
00:13:36,065 --> 00:13:39,985
Don't give your teachers a headache.

268
00:13:40,069 --> 00:13:41,111
[in English] Okay?

269
00:13:41,195 --> 00:13:42,321
Go ahead.

270
00:13:42,404 --> 00:13:44,907
Eat this. He said it's delicious.
[chuckles]

271
00:13:45,616 --> 00:13:46,742
There you go.

272
00:13:53,582 --> 00:13:56,001
He really doesn't want to see me, huh?

273
00:13:57,419 --> 00:14:01,465
Because he wasn't the one waiting for me.

274
00:14:01,549 --> 00:14:02,883
[somber music playing]

275
00:14:02,967 --> 00:14:04,927
Uh, uh-- No.

276
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:09,932
It's because he has a big mission,

277
00:14:10,015 --> 00:14:12,268
so it's difficult.

278
00:14:12,768 --> 00:14:14,186
And he said

279
00:14:14,270 --> 00:14:18,107
you should pray for him
to San Antonio de Padua, so

280
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:20,150
he can find and get what he needs

281
00:14:20,234 --> 00:14:22,319
and he can come home safely to us.

282
00:14:24,530 --> 00:14:25,948
Emerson, we'll go ahead, okay.

283
00:14:26,031 --> 00:14:27,700
- The child might be late.
- Yes, okay.

284
00:14:27,783 --> 00:14:29,577
- Oh, all right.
- Oh, go ahead. All right.

285
00:14:30,160 --> 00:14:31,287
[in English] Bye-bye!

286
00:14:34,164 --> 00:14:36,959
[bright music playing]

287
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:09,617
Please give this to him.

288
00:15:09,700 --> 00:15:14,830
Tell him to read it
before he does his mission.

289
00:15:15,497 --> 00:15:19,001
If not, I'll be even angrier.

290
00:15:19,668 --> 00:15:22,379
I walked so far,
I thought you were following me.

291
00:15:22,463 --> 00:15:24,673
Come on. You'll be late.

292
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:26,842
Okay. Sure, I'll deliver it.

293
00:15:27,635 --> 00:15:28,469
Take care, okay?

294
00:15:28,552 --> 00:15:30,554
Oh, come on. I'll do it. Come on.

295
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:34,224
You're late. I walked so far already.

296
00:15:35,601 --> 00:15:37,895
- [music fades]
- [sewing machine whirring]

297
00:15:40,648 --> 00:15:44,318
[soft rock music playing]

298
00:15:49,114 --> 00:15:51,200
Where did you lose your ID badge, Ben?

299
00:15:51,283 --> 00:15:53,827
[Ben] <i>If I knew,</i>
<i>I would've found it already.</i>

300
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:03,337
<i>How long does it take to replace it?</i>

301
00:16:03,420 --> 00:16:07,132
[security guard] <i>I'll just notify</i>
<i>my replacement at the service entrance.</i>

302
00:16:08,550 --> 00:16:10,928
[Ben] <i>Just make sure</i>
<i>the spelling is correct.</i>

303
00:16:11,011 --> 00:16:14,139
<i>Ben Laput. It's letter U, not letter O.</i>

304
00:16:16,100 --> 00:16:19,687
[music fades]

305
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:20,729
[Emerson] Atoy!

306
00:16:21,647 --> 00:16:22,815
Oh?

307
00:16:22,898 --> 00:16:24,149
Is it good? Mm.

308
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:27,277
[whimsical music playing]

309
00:16:27,361 --> 00:16:28,821
What's with the look?

310
00:16:28,904 --> 00:16:29,822
Of course.

311
00:16:29,905 --> 00:16:31,657
I want to show you that…

312
00:16:31,740 --> 00:16:33,575
I'm better than Brother Kurt.

313
00:16:33,659 --> 00:16:34,743
Especially when it comes to disguises,

314
00:16:34,827 --> 00:16:37,246
so you'll always bring me
on your missions.

315
00:16:37,329 --> 00:16:38,789
Right? Mm.

316
00:16:38,872 --> 00:16:39,873
- I look like--
- You're even wearing a leather jacket

317
00:16:39,957 --> 00:16:40,833
and gloves. What for--

318
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:43,669
Well, of course, race car driver style.

319
00:16:43,752 --> 00:16:46,005
Race car driver? You look like a goon.

320
00:16:46,088 --> 00:16:47,339
- Huh?
- Take it off!

321
00:16:47,423 --> 00:16:49,383
That's not needed. Too-- Too over the top.

322
00:16:49,466 --> 00:16:50,509
We'll get noticed.

323
00:16:50,592 --> 00:16:52,011
Take it off?

324
00:16:52,803 --> 00:16:53,721
It should be simple.

325
00:16:53,804 --> 00:16:55,806
I even worked hard to look like this.

326
00:16:55,889 --> 00:16:57,891
You. Fine. Oh.

327
00:16:57,975 --> 00:16:58,851
Okay.

328
00:16:58,934 --> 00:17:01,520
By the way, here.

329
00:17:01,603 --> 00:17:02,771
[music fades]

330
00:17:02,855 --> 00:17:04,732
Ibyang asked me to give this.

331
00:17:06,108 --> 00:17:07,192
[Emerson] Mm-hmm.

332
00:17:08,485 --> 00:17:10,320
This look is different, huh.

333
00:17:10,904 --> 00:17:11,822
Right?

334
00:17:12,322 --> 00:17:13,991
Here, even the gloves.

335
00:17:14,074 --> 00:17:16,702
[bright music playing]

336
00:17:16,785 --> 00:17:18,871
Ibyang said we should be careful,

337
00:17:18,954 --> 00:17:21,457
because if something bad happens to me,

338
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:24,501
she won't talk to me for 20 million years.

339
00:17:24,585 --> 00:17:25,419
[Emerson giggles]

340
00:17:25,502 --> 00:17:27,129
So, we need to be careful.

341
00:17:27,212 --> 00:17:29,631
Oh, well… To be sure,

342
00:17:30,382 --> 00:17:34,136
I'll block the person
whose face you copied.

343
00:17:34,219 --> 00:17:37,681
Yes, I need Ben to be gone
for about three hours,

344
00:17:37,765 --> 00:17:39,475
so I can do what I need to do.

345
00:17:40,100 --> 00:17:41,185
Three?!

346
00:17:41,268 --> 00:17:42,561
Three hours?!

347
00:17:43,145 --> 00:17:44,605
What will I do for three hours there?

348
00:17:44,688 --> 00:17:46,356
What, sew him a barong?

349
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:49,151
What, give him a manicure and pedicure
just to keep him there?

350
00:17:49,234 --> 00:17:51,111
- Three hours is long, Atoy.
- You can do it.

351
00:17:51,195 --> 00:17:52,696
Just listen carefully.

352
00:17:53,822 --> 00:17:56,909
Ben will arrive before two o'clock.

353
00:17:56,992 --> 00:17:58,535
Okay? Then, when I enter,

354
00:17:59,244 --> 00:18:04,416
I'll probably need at least
two hours to get the device.

355
00:18:04,917 --> 00:18:06,085
So, listen carefully.

356
00:18:06,168 --> 00:18:09,004
Our planned coordination,
you can't mess up.

357
00:18:09,088 --> 00:18:09,963
- Okay, fine.
- [in English] Copy?

358
00:18:10,047 --> 00:18:11,924
[in English] Copy. Oh, from the top.

359
00:18:12,007 --> 00:18:13,092
Go ahead. Come again?

360
00:18:13,717 --> 00:18:14,843
No. Go ahead, tell me. I'll remember it.

361
00:18:14,927 --> 00:18:16,220
- Three hours.
- Three hours. Okay?

362
00:18:16,303 --> 00:18:17,554
Just three hours. Find a way.

363
00:18:17,638 --> 00:18:19,348
Whatever it takes. Block him.

364
00:18:19,431 --> 00:18:21,767
[inaudible]

365
00:18:21,850 --> 00:18:23,185
[birds chirping]

366
00:18:23,268 --> 00:18:25,020
Where's the party, Dad?

367
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:27,606
[in English] I was invited
by a good friend of mine.

368
00:18:27,689 --> 00:18:29,483
[in English] He's kind of a big deal.

369
00:18:29,983 --> 00:18:32,611
Unless you're busy or…

370
00:18:32,694 --> 00:18:34,196
you have plans with Atoy.

371
00:18:35,948 --> 00:18:36,990
Not really.

372
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:40,244
[in English] Um, he'll be preoccupied
for the next few days.

373
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:52,172
[sighs] Child…

374
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:57,344
Are you really sure about Atoy?

375
00:18:57,427 --> 00:18:58,512
[suspicious music playing]

376
00:18:58,595 --> 00:19:00,514
[in English] What are you
trying to say, Dad?

377
00:19:00,597 --> 00:19:02,558
[in English] All I'm saying is…

378
00:19:04,518 --> 00:19:08,772
You know that Atoy's work
as a tracker is dangerous.

379
00:19:09,648 --> 00:19:12,067
You and your daughter
might get caught up in it.

380
00:19:13,443 --> 00:19:15,487
Dad, be honest with me.

381
00:19:16,363 --> 00:19:18,949
You don't want Atoy for me, do you?

382
00:19:21,952 --> 00:19:25,873
[in English] I'm just worried about you
and my grandchild.

383
00:19:26,665 --> 00:19:29,168
Atoy is a good man.

384
00:19:30,419 --> 00:19:32,629
[in English] Everyone has a secret, child.

385
00:19:34,214 --> 00:19:36,216
Especially someone like Atoy.

386
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:41,805
[in English] I just want you
to be careful.

387
00:19:42,598 --> 00:19:43,432
[in English] Always.

388
00:19:45,642 --> 00:19:46,643
[in English] Okay?

389
00:19:52,941 --> 00:19:54,401
[music fades]

390
00:19:55,152 --> 00:19:58,989
[rousing music playing]

391
00:20:03,410 --> 00:20:06,830
[Atoy] <i>I'll position myself</i>
<i>near the entrance, right side.</i>

392
00:20:06,914 --> 00:20:07,998
<i>Okay?</i>

393
00:20:08,081 --> 00:20:09,875
<i>Watch for Ben on the left.</i>

394
00:20:10,584 --> 00:20:12,753
<i>That's where he'll come from.</i>

395
00:20:12,836 --> 00:20:14,922
This must be it. This is it.

396
00:20:15,005 --> 00:20:20,302
[Atoy] <i>When you see Ben, act drunk</i>
<i>and like you've known him for a long time.</i>

397
00:20:20,385 --> 00:20:21,637
<i>That's the acting.</i>

398
00:20:21,720 --> 00:20:22,721
Ben, my friend!

399
00:20:23,513 --> 00:20:24,431
[Atoy] <i>You have to be persistent!</i>

400
00:20:24,514 --> 00:20:27,184
Ben, my friend! Ben, my friend!

401
00:20:27,267 --> 00:20:29,102
Hey! How are you?

402
00:20:29,686 --> 00:20:31,897
[chuckles] What's the news, my friend?

403
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:33,023
Oh?

404
00:20:33,565 --> 00:20:34,691
How are you?

405
00:20:34,775 --> 00:20:35,943
Do we know each other?

406
00:20:36,026 --> 00:20:37,110
Hey, yes!

407
00:20:37,194 --> 00:20:40,697
We even bumped
into each other at the market recently!

408
00:20:40,781 --> 00:20:42,074
- So, what's up?
- Huh? When was that?

409
00:20:42,157 --> 00:20:45,077
[Atoy] <i>Once you've got him, I'll go in.</i>

410
00:20:45,160 --> 00:20:45,994
<i>That's it.</i>

411
00:20:46,078 --> 00:20:47,287
[soft rock music playing]

412
00:20:47,371 --> 00:20:50,123
- At the market, and--
- Huh? When?

413
00:20:50,207 --> 00:20:52,417
[music swells]

414
00:20:55,879 --> 00:20:59,132
[music fades]

415
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:03,845
- [tense music playing]
- [sighs]

416
00:21:03,929 --> 00:21:05,347
Still him?

417
00:21:06,098 --> 00:21:07,683
[in English] What did you say?

418
00:21:07,766 --> 00:21:09,559
[in English] You can't get over
that businessman

419
00:21:09,643 --> 00:21:11,603
because of what he did to your face, huh?

420
00:21:11,687 --> 00:21:13,063
[suspicious music playing]

421
00:21:13,146 --> 00:21:14,231
[clamoring]

422
00:21:14,314 --> 00:21:15,190
[Kurt gasps]

423
00:21:15,274 --> 00:21:17,109
- [in English] Alexei! What are you doing
- [in English] Brother!

424
00:21:17,192 --> 00:21:18,610
to my brother, huh?!

425
00:21:18,694 --> 00:21:20,654
[in English] Your brother
is the one who hit me first!

426
00:21:21,488 --> 00:21:22,656
[in English] Yes.

427
00:21:24,283 --> 00:21:26,410
[in English] Everyone is in position.

428
00:21:26,493 --> 00:21:29,288
[in English] The ambassador's guests
for the party will be here soon.

429
00:21:29,371 --> 00:21:30,706
[in English] Look at him.

430
00:21:30,789 --> 00:21:33,041
[suspicious music playing]

431
00:21:33,125 --> 00:21:36,712
[in English] Does it look like
he's looking for the bathroom?

432
00:21:37,921 --> 00:21:38,839
Hmm?

433
00:21:39,756 --> 00:21:42,301
[in English] It looks like
he wants to go into the office.

434
00:21:44,678 --> 00:21:46,847
[in English] I want you
to check his profile.

435
00:21:46,930 --> 00:21:50,767
[in English] His name is Alexei Sokolov.

436
00:21:52,311 --> 00:21:53,478
[in English] Okay, sir.

437
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:56,189
[tense music playing]

438
00:22:00,027 --> 00:22:01,862
[woman] Samir got hit
right on the forehead.

439
00:22:01,945 --> 00:22:03,405
- Oh?
- [woman] Yes.

440
00:22:03,488 --> 00:22:05,866
- He even looked cross-eyed, that fool.
- [chuckles]

441
00:22:05,949 --> 00:22:07,326
He is arrogant.

442
00:22:07,409 --> 00:22:08,744
Too bad I didn't see his face.

443
00:22:08,827 --> 00:22:10,537
- [chuckles]
- Like this?

444
00:22:10,620 --> 00:22:12,497
[chuckles]

445
00:22:12,581 --> 00:22:19,004
But Samir said he'll look
for the businessman he fought with.

446
00:22:19,087 --> 00:22:20,547
What do you think he plans to do?

447
00:22:20,630 --> 00:22:22,632
[woman] Hmm, maybe he wants
to even the score.

448
00:22:22,716 --> 00:22:24,509
[laughs]

449
00:22:24,593 --> 00:22:26,386
Maybe. Thank you, sir.

450
00:22:26,470 --> 00:22:27,429
[woman] Thank you!

451
00:22:27,512 --> 00:22:29,931
[suspicious music playing]

452
00:22:30,015 --> 00:22:33,143
Bro, is this where
you get the replacement ID?

453
00:22:33,769 --> 00:22:34,770
What's your name?

454
00:22:35,687 --> 00:22:36,521
Ben Laput.

455
00:22:36,605 --> 00:22:39,191
Uh, Laput. Letter U, not letter O.

456
00:22:40,567 --> 00:22:43,278
There's a Ben Laput here,
claiming an ID badge.

457
00:22:43,361 --> 00:22:44,946
[radio static]

458
00:22:45,030 --> 00:22:46,656
[security guard] <i>The one</i>
<i>with the scar on his face?</i>

459
00:22:46,740 --> 00:22:47,991
<i>That's our window cleaner.</i>

460
00:22:48,075 --> 00:22:49,993
[radio static]

461
00:22:59,169 --> 00:23:01,922
[music fades]

462
00:23:02,005 --> 00:23:03,757
[tense music playing]

463
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:05,467
Is that still necessary, boss?

464
00:23:05,550 --> 00:23:07,260
We've got a lot of work to do.

465
00:23:07,344 --> 00:23:08,595
We're in a hurry.

466
00:23:15,644 --> 00:23:17,145
[security guard] Is this your bag?

467
00:23:17,229 --> 00:23:18,105
Yes.

468
00:23:18,814 --> 00:23:19,773
[Atoy clears throat]

469
00:23:20,273 --> 00:23:22,651
[music swells]

470
00:23:22,734 --> 00:23:25,195
[device beeping]

471
00:23:25,278 --> 00:23:26,613
What are you carrying here?

472
00:23:26,696 --> 00:23:30,534
[intense music playing]

473
00:23:32,410 --> 00:23:36,456
- [electronic blipping]
- [tense music playing]

474
00:23:42,754 --> 00:23:44,673
UP NEXT

475
00:23:46,925 --> 00:23:48,385
I-I just wanted to let you know

476
00:23:48,468 --> 00:23:51,471
I'm here now at the embassy of Zahran.

477
00:23:51,555 --> 00:23:54,599
[Atoy] What?! What are you doing
here at the embassy?

478
00:23:58,311 --> 00:24:00,355
How long will you keep avoiding Atoy?

479
00:24:00,438 --> 00:24:02,774
I can't face Brother Atoy
because I feel guilty.

480
00:24:02,858 --> 00:24:04,526
But you didn't do anything wrong.

481
00:24:04,609 --> 00:24:06,194
I'm not like you guys who have thick skin.

482
00:24:07,028 --> 00:24:11,032
["Mr. Tailor" playing]

483
00:24:12,659 --> 00:24:13,743
♪ <i>Oh, Mr. Tailor</i> ♪

484
00:24:13,827 --> 00:24:15,787
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i> ♪

485
00:24:15,871 --> 00:24:19,708
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

486
00:24:19,791 --> 00:24:21,543
‪♪ <i>‪Fix it</i>‪ ♪

487
00:24:21,626 --> 00:24:22,627
Subtitle translation by: Rachel C. Arias
